==Battleground==
*4 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
*3 [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 80~83.33 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,500f</sup>.
*4 [[Zigge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 93.33~96.67 seconds<sup>2,800f~2,900f</sup>.
*4 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Emperor Warumongar]] spawns as the boss after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Enchanting Mage Vibon]] spawns after 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>.
*2 [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*3 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 156.67 seconds<sup>4,700f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The opposition is getting desperate, this may yet be their last stand! Bring [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] to tank (though it is generally recommended to use [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] over Ramen Cat if available). [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] all cover DPS. The only Nyanko Rangers worth considering for this stage are [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Red Nyanko Ranger]] for Emperor Warumongar, as well as [[Commander Cat (Special Cat)|Gold Nyanko Ranger]] and [[Barista Cat (Special Cat)|Silver Nyanko Ranger]] for [[Gold Silver Strike (Combo)|Gold Silver Strike]].

Take out the horde of Zombies, then stall Warumongar and Vibon until Lutrinae Gokurakko spawns. Use a well-timed [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]/[[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]] to instantly take the first one out. The Gokurakkos are basically the only threatening presence here with actual pushing power, so you can passively keep the siblings locked in place while actively dealing with burrowing Zombies at your own pace. Bahamut won't be off cooldown by the time the second Gokurakko spawns, so deal with this one by repeatedly cycling out Mushroom Cats and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cats]] until it dies. You have a lot of space to work with, which means you can leverage some of it to push and pull the enemies to your liking. Use Awakened Bahamut Cat on the second Aku Gory, then relax because you've basically won the stage once it dies. Cleanup is a breeze, as you can slowly wear down the boss duo with Can Cans, Jelly Dumplings, and Nyanko Rangers.

